  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/sports-ontology#PierluigiCollina">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/sports-ontology#Referee" />
    <sport:level>International</sport:level>
    <sport:firstName>Pierluigi</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Collina</sport:lastName>
    <sport:nationality>Italy</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">29</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:matchesOfficiated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">430</sport:matchesOfficiated>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1960-02-13</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:description>Widely regarded as the greatest referee of all time, Pierluigi Collina officiated the 2002 World Cup Final and multiple Champions League finals. His distinctive bald appearance and authoritative presence commanded respect from players and coaches alike. Known for his exceptional decision-making, consistency, and ability to control high-pressure matches, he set the standard for modern refereeing.</sport:description>
    <sport:expertise>Match control, Consistency, Communication, Decision-making under pressure, Authority</sport:expertise>
  </rdf:Description>
